      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/robins_iowa",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Cedar Rapids & Chicago Railroad right-of-way was granted through Robins in 1887, boosting market connectivity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/robins_iowa",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Robins' settlement began in the late 19th century as a rural community focused on agriculture, thanks to fertile lands and its proximity to Cedar Rapids.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/robins_iowa",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Robins lies about 5 miles south of the Cedar River valley, a factor that shapes regional hydrology and can lead to occasional flood risks.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/robins_iowa",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "School zoning in Robins includes Hiawatha and Nixon elementary schools, as well as Harding Middle School and Kennedy High School.",
